# Copy this to `.npmrc` next to your package.json and COMMIT it.
#
# There is no secret here — only the name of an environment variable, which npm
# expands at install time. The token itself stays in your shell profile.
#
# Why this file is needed at all: GitHub Packages requires a token even to READ,
# and even for a public package. Without these two lines npm looks for @noduf on
# npmjs.org, does not find it, and reports a 404 that says nothing about the
# actual cause.

@noduf:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
